{"id": "e97", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding GitHub", "quote": "In VS Code, it solved more terminal tasks than Opus 5 in less than half the steps."}
{"id": "e98", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding Optiver", "quote": "On our agentic coding tasks, Claude Opus 5.5 matched Opus 5’s quality in about half the turns, time and output tokens, cutting the cost of that workload by 40 to 50%."}
{"id": "e99", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding Kiro", "quote": "On a public benchmark of real command-line tasks, Claude Opus 5.5 solved more than Opus 5 while making about 40% fewer calls and using half the tokens."}
{"id": "e100", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding Lovable", "quote": "finishing in a third to half fewer steps and using significantly fewer tokens along the way."}
{"id": "e101", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Coding Quantium", "quote": "A complex coding task that previously took 38 prompts over four days came in at 11 prompts over three hours, with more production-ready outputs and less rework."}
{"id": "e102", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2 p83", "quote": "Auto mode, now the default permission mode in Claude Code for most of our users, is an additional line of defense. It pairs these prompt injection probes with a classifier that blocks potentially dangerous tool calls"}
{"id": "e103", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.1 p85", "quote": "All models are evaluated without the prompt injection protections we deploy in our products to assess changes across models."}
{"id": "e104", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The most secure coding agent", "quote": "Opus 5.5 has a classifier that screens every action before it runs, an open-source sandbox that security teams can audit, and code review that catches vulnerabilities before they merge."}
{"id": "e105", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2 p83", "quote": "Within each of these evaluations, Claude Opus 5.5 matched or improved on Claude Opus 5, making it our most robust Opus-class model to date."}
{"id": "e106", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.2.1 p88", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5’s attack success rate is driven by the cyber classifier fallback."}
{"id": "e107", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.2.1 p87", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 substantially improves on Claude Opus 5 in coding environments against this stronger attacker, with an attack success rate of 54.61% over all attempts"}
{"id": "e108", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.2.1 p88", "quote": "Of the requests that received a valid response, 64% of those sent to Claude Opus 5.5 were served by Claude Opus 4.8, compared to the 60% fallback rate for Claude Fable 5.1 and 14% for Claude Opus 5 with thinking enabled."}
{"id": "e109", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.1 p85", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 matches Claude Fable 5.1, our most robust model to date on this benchmark, with an attack success rate of 0.1% at k=1, 0.7% at k=10, and 1.0% at k=15. This improves on Claude Opus 5 (0.4%, 3.6%, and 4.8%, respectively)."}
{"id": "e110", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.1 p86", "quote": "Fallbacks do not degrade robustness on this benchmark: none of the 1,310 fallback-served rollouts resulted in a successful attack."}
{"id": "e111", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.2.1 p88", "quote": "whereas Claude Sonnet 5 remains the most robust model without probes (19.47% with thinking)."}
{"id": "e112", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.2 p86", "quote": "They reflect a deliberately permissive threat model: the attacker optimizes directly against the test scenarios and is given many attempts per scenario."}
{"id": "e113", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.5.1 p126", "quote": "Following the updated training, the final version of Claude Opus 5.5 acted on the planted instruction in about 2% of attempts at its default reasoning effort and about 7.4% at max effort."}
{"id": "e114", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.5.1 p126", "quote": "With product mitigations in place, the model did not follow any visible or invisible planted instructions."}
{"id": "e115", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.5.1 p126", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 acted in two of the 68 invisible-character attempts at its default reasoning effort."}
{"id": "e116", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.5.1 p126", "quote": "the model never acted on the planted instructions when they arrived within tool results (0 of 105 attempts)"}
{"id": "e117", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.5.1 p124", "quote": "The rubric explicitly stated that instructions in the user prompt should never be flagged."}
{"id": "e118", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.5.1 p123", "quote": "In the transcripts we analyzed, Claude Opus 5.5 often reasoned that anything in the user’s message must come from the user and could not be a prompt injection, and therefore should be followed."}
{"id": "e119", "source": "d7", "locator": "§Mark pasted text in user messages", "quote": "Wrap each pasted block in an opening and a closing tag that both carry the same short random ID, generated by your application, with each tag on its own line:"}
{"id": "e120", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Knowledge work", "quote": "Across different effort settings, 16 out of 18 of Opus 5.5’s reports cleared our quality bar, where any invented figure or quote would have failed. Neither Fable 5.1 nor Opus 5 cleared that bar in any attempt."}
