{"id": "e146", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication bug", "quote": "The extra drop isn’t the free tier — it’s a regression in 0552feb"}
{"id": "e147", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication bug", "quote": "The free-tier change accounts for only $1.50 of acme’s August drop. The other $9.92 comes from a bug in commit 0552feb."}
{"id": "e148", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication bug", "quote": "The usage isn’t moved to another month; it’s never billed at all."}
{"id": "e149", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication thread", "quote": "The ops dashboard tile that depended on the Friday file now reads from the live table (Sam, done). A failure alert now pages the on-call channel (Priya, done and tested)."}
{"id": "e150", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication design", "quote": "One matrix multiply with the board's occupancy counts the blockers on every line at once, and an attack survives only if that count is zero."}
{"id": "e151", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication Box", "quote": "In our evaluations, Claude Opus 5.5 used a third of the tokens Opus 5 did, and its answers were 40% less verbose without losing accuracy."}
{"id": "e152", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication Factory", "quote": "In our testing it matched Opus 5 on high effort, while using 20 to 25% fewer output tokens."}
{"id": "e153", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Communication", "quote": "It puts the most important information up front, is less likely to use jargon or idiosyncratic phrases, and follows the writing rules you give it."}
{"id": "e154", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "It was tested before release by external evaluators, including Frontier Design"}
{"id": "e155", "source": "n2", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "This is the key step for verifiability of any pacing commitments, and has precedent in the banking industry, which sometimes involves regulatory “supervisors” embedded along with employees. Anthropic is unilaterally committing to this step now."}
{"id": "e156", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Pacing the frontier", "quote": "For these models, we do not assume the measures described above will meet that safety standard on their own."}
{"id": "e157", "source": "n2", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "To be clear, pacing does not mean halting model training or technical progress, but ensuring companies take adequate time to align and safeguard their models, and for third party evaluators to confirm this."}
{"id": "e158", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.4.8 p119", "quote": "comprising 28 handmade scenarios tailored to elicit sandbox escape, run seven times for each model."}
{"id": "e159", "source": "s1", "locator": "Figure 6.4.8.A p119 (렌더링)", "quote": "Sandbox escape attempted crossings, low-severity / moderate-and-above: Claude Mythos 5 14.9% / 9.3%, Claude Opus 5 7.7% / 2.6%, Claude Mythos 5.1 8.7% / 1.0%, Claude Opus 5.5 1.5% / none shown"}
{"id": "e160", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Alignment", "quote": "We see signs that Opus 5.5 often suspects it is being evaluated, which challenges our ability to assess how it will act in the vast variety of real-world settings it is deployed in."}
{"id": "e161", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Alignment", "quote": "Opus 5.5 attempted to circumvent boundaries around 85% less often than Opus 5 or Claude Mythos 5.1, and every attempt it made was low severity and self-reported."}
{"id": "e162", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Alignment", "quote": "On our primary evaluation suite, an automated behavioral audit that assesses Claude across nearly 2,000 scenarios, Opus 5.5 scored better than any recent Claude model on nearly every measure of misaligned behavior."}
{"id": "e163", "source": "s1", "locator": "Executive Summary p3", "quote": "Regressions included being more likely to follow malicious instructions planted in text a user pastes into their own prompt, more often accepting unverifiable claims of authorization, and being more evasive on sensitive questions than Claude Mythos-class models."}
{"id": "e164", "source": "s1", "locator": "Executive Summary p3", "quote": "when given apparent credentials to a public package registry in a simulated security exercise, took potentially harmful actions in roughly half of cases."}
{"id": "e165", "source": "s1", "locator": "§1.5 p13", "quote": "Our blocking classifiers for development of conventional weapons and high-yield explosives behave similarly to previous models like Claude Fable 5.1 and do not have a fallback model."}
{"id": "e166", "source": "s1", "locator": "§1.5 p13", "quote": "Our classifiers to prevent distillation of our models (for example, by attempting to extract a model’s hidden reasoning) will block on Claude Opus 5.5 with no fallback model."}
{"id": "e167", "source": "d8", "locator": "§How refusals are billed", "quote": "a refusal that arrives before any output is billed when its `stop_details.category` is `\"bio\"`, `\"frontier_llm\"`, or `\"reasoning_extraction\"`."}
{"id": "e168", "source": "d8", "locator": "§How refusals are billed", "quote": "A refusal before any output in any other category, or with a `null` category, is not billed."}
{"id": "e169", "source": "d8", "locator": "§How refusals are billed", "quote": "Either way, `content` is empty and token counts appear in `usage`. The request still counts against your rate limits."}
{"id": "e170", "source": "d8", "locator": "§refusal category table", "quote": "| `\"cyber\"`                | The request could enable cyber harm, such as malware or exploit development. Benign cybersecurity work can also trigger this category.                                                                                                    | No                       |"}
{"id": "e171", "source": "d4", "locator": "§Switching models", "quote": "On the Claude API, Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1 read thinking blocks from Claude Opus 5.5; no other model does."}
{"id": "e172", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "When a request carries a block the target model can't read, the API drops it before the model sees it: the request succeeds, and dropped blocks aren't billed."}
{"id": "e173", "source": "d8", "locator": "§Server-side fallback", "quote": "The `fallbacks` parameter is not supported on the [Message Batches API](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/batch-processing) (a batch item that includes it comes back as an errored result) and is not available on Amazon Bedrock, Google Cloud, or Microsoft Foundry."}
{"id": "e174", "source": "s1", "locator": "§1.5 p13", "quote": "The fallback behavior described above applies to our first-party products and developers who are opted in to such fallbacks on our API; traffic on our models via other platforms and providers may experience different behavior."}
{"id": "e175", "source": "s1", "locator": "§3.4 p55", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 will allow vulnerability discovery in source code at all access levels, including general availability, while continuing to block vulnerability discovery in compiled binaries."}
{"id": "e176", "source": "s1", "locator": "Figure 3.4.2.A p57 (렌더링)", "quote": "Defensive vulnerability discovery, classifier flag rate (lower is better): Claude Sonnet 5 3.2%, Claude Opus 5 13.9%, Claude Fable 5.1 7.0%, Claude Opus 5.5 4.5%"}
{"id": "e177", "source": "h2", "locator": "§top note", "quote": "Note: This article applies only to Opus and Sonnet class models, but doesn’t apply to Claude Opus 5.5 or Sonnet 5.5."}
{"id": "e178", "source": "h2", "locator": "§Cyber Verification Program", "quote": "Organizations on Zero Data Retention (ZDR) are not currently eligible to participate in the CVP."}
{"id": "e179", "source": "h2", "locator": "§How to apply", "quote": "The Cyber Verification Program is not available on Bedrock at this time."}
{"id": "e180", "source": "s1", "locator": "§3.2 p48", "quote": "Given that Claude Opus 5.5’s cyber capabilities are comparable to Claude Mythos 5.1, we have opted for a temporarily wider safety margin against jailbreaks while we continuously work to improve the robustness of our classifiers"}
{"id": "e181", "source": "s1", "locator": "§3.2 p48", "quote": "First, a probe looks at Claude’s internal activations, screening all traffic and escalating any traffic that it flags as cyber related. Second, the escalated traffic is scored by a lightweight classifier running on Claude Opus 5.5 itself."}
{"id": "e182", "source": "s1", "locator": "§1.5 p12", "quote": "For chemical and biological (CB) risks, we have deployed the same research biology classifiers in use for our deployments of Claude Fable 5 and Claude Fable 5.1."}
{"id": "e183", "source": "n1", "locator": "§How monitoring works in LSVP", "quote": "For LSVP traffic, we are requiring data retention for 30 days to be able to do this monitoring effectively."}
{"id": "e184", "source": "n1", "locator": "§Verification and access types", "quote": "These grants can be extended to entire teams for diverse, daily workloads, and are renewed once a year."}
{"id": "e185", "source": "n1", "locator": "§Verification and access types", "quote": "It removes all safeguards that block life sciences requests. This grant applies to a single research project as opposed to a full team, and must be renewed every six months."}
{"id": "e186", "source": "n1", "locator": "§Verification and access types", "quote": "Standard Use grants apply to Mythos 5.1, Opus 5, and Sonnet 5 today, and to future models as they launch."}
{"id": "e187", "source": "n1", "locator": "§Verification and access types", "quote": "High-risk grants for Claude Opus 5 and Claude Sonnet 5 are available today."}
{"id": "e188", "source": "n1", "locator": "§Applications and availability", "quote": "As a beta, LSVP is not available for BAA-enabled orgs."}
{"id": "e189", "source": "n1", "locator": "§Applications and availability", "quote": "We do not yet support individual plans but are working to expand access for these users. It is also not yet available on third-party platforms."}
{"id": "e190", "source": "n1", "locator": "§Verification and access types", "quote": "All other safeguards, such as cyber classifiers, will remain in place under LSVP grants."}
{"id": "e191", "source": "d4", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "The API enforces the prefix check by default for accounts created on or after August 31, 2026, 00:00 UTC."}
{"id": "e192", "source": "d4", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "If the prefix differs from what you sent when the block was produced, that block and every later thinking block are invalid, and the API rejects the request with a 400 error or drops the invalid blocks, whichever you choose."}
{"id": "e193", "source": "d4", "locator": "§Who needs to change anything", "quote": "On an older account, none of these produces an error unless the request sets `prefix_mismatch_behavior`, so a run with no errors on your own key doesn't show whether your code is affected."}
{"id": "e194", "source": "d4", "locator": "§Who needs to change anything", "quote": "If people run your tool with their own API keys, those on newer accounts get the 400 error before you do."}
{"id": "e195", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "To drop the affected blocks instead, send the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta header and set `thinking.block_binding.prefix_mismatch_behavior` to `\"drop_block\"`."}
{"id": "e196", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "With the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta header the drop is reported in a top-level `input_transformations` array."}
{"id": "e197", "source": "d4", "locator": "§Who needs to change anything", "quote": "Nothing changes for you if Claude Code, claude.ai, Claude Managed Agents, or the Claude Agent SDK builds your requests"}
{"id": "e198", "source": "d4", "locator": "§Who needs to change anything", "quote": "the date, a mode flag, re-read project instructions, or a plugin or MCP server that connects after the first turn"}
{"id": "e199", "source": "h1", "locator": "§What does this mean for API integrations?", "quote": "It replaces client-side compaction, which is likely the most common reason integrations need to change."}
{"id": "e200", "source": "h1", "locator": "§Thinking can only be read by the account that created it", "quote": "Starting with Claude Sonnet 5.5, a thinking block can only be read by the account that created it, or by an account linked to it."}
{"id": "e201", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Data retention and compliance", "quote": "Like previous Opus models, Opus 5.5 is available with zero data retention."}
{"id": "e202", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Data retention and compliance", "quote": "As with Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5 comes with our watermarking measures to comply with the EU AI Act, discussed here"}
{"id": "e203", "source": "h2", "locator": "§Enable data retention on Claude on Google Cloud", "quote": "In order to access the Cyber Verification Program through Claude on Google Cloud, you must consent to and configure data retention."}
{"id": "e204", "source": "d1", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "Four breaking changes affect code already running on Claude Opus 5:"}
{"id": "e205", "source": "d1", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "A further change alters the response shape without failing any request:"}
{"id": "e206", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Behavior differences", "quote": "The short notes the model writes between tool calls arrive as [progress-update `thinking` blocks](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking#progress-updates) rather than `text` blocks"}
{"id": "e207", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking can't be disabled", "quote": "select content blocks by their `type` field rather than by position"}
{"id": "e208", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Behavior differences", "quote": "The model runs a biology safety classifier in addition to the cybersecurity one, and requests that push it to reproduce its internal reasoning in the response text can be declined with the `reasoning_extraction` category."}
{"id": "e209", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking can't be disabled", "quote": "lower it where you previously disabled thinking"}
{"id": "e210", "source": "d5", "locator": "§Recommended effort levels for Claude Opus 5.5", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 also supports [changing effort mid-conversation](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/effort#change-effort-mid-conversation-beta) with a per-message `output_config`, which preserves the prompt cache."}
{"id": "e211", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Availability", "quote": "Claude in Amazon Bedrock](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/claude-in-amazon-bedrock), as `anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`"}
{"id": "e212", "source": "d3", "locator": "§notes", "quote": "On the Message Batches API, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Opus 5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Opus 4.6, and Claude Sonnet 4.6 support up to 300k output tokens with the output-300k-2026-03-24 beta header."}
{"id": "e213", "source": "d5", "locator": "§Recommended effort levels for Claude Opus 5.5", "quote": "set a large `max_tokens` at the higher levels: it's a hard limit on total output (thinking plus response text)."}
{"id": "e214", "source": "hn49804862", "locator": "comment 49804862 (simonw, 2026-09-22T17:22:51Z)", "quote": "I haven't managed to get one for level \"max\" yet, it hit the limit of 128,000 cap for output tokens while it was still reasoning about the question!"}
{"id": "e215", "source": "s1", "locator": "§8.14.5 Table 8.14.5.A p211", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5                  77.8               82.4               72.2               26.9"}
{"id": "e216", "source": "s1", "locator": "§8.14.5 Table 8.14.5.A p211", "quote": "Claude Opus 5                    80.6               87.0               73.1               23.5"}
{"id": "e217", "source": "s1", "locator": "§8.14.5 p210", "quote": "Of 324 trials, one trial (0.3%) was stopped by production safety classifiers and six (1.9%) were halted by our evaluation harness's sandbox-escape monitor, and all seven are counted as failures."}
{"id": "e218", "source": "s1", "locator": "Executive Summary p4", "quote": "It scored higher on every evaluation in our capability summary (Table 8.1.A), with the largest gains in agentic coding, visual reasoning, computer use, and long-horizon professional knowledge work."}
