{"id": "e224", "source": "d8", "locator": "§Server-side fallback", "quote": "is not available on Amazon Bedrock, Google Cloud, or Microsoft Foundry. On those platforms, use [client-side fallback with the SDK middleware]"}
{"id": "e225", "source": "d8", "locator": "§Sticky routing", "quote": "Later requests for that conversation that include `fallbacks` go directly to that fallback model, without running the requested model."}
{"id": "e226", "source": "d8", "locator": "§Sticky routing", "quote": "It is retained for approximately 1 hour and is scoped to your organization."}
{"id": "e227", "source": "d8", "locator": "§Billing and rate limits", "quote": "Each attempt follows the rules in [How refusals are billed](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#how-refusals-are-billed), at the rates of the model that ran it."}
{"id": "e228", "source": "d2", "locator": "§Model pricing", "quote": "| Claude Opus 4.8                                                                                                                       | $5 / MTok             | $6.25 / MTok    | $10 / MTok      | $0.50 / MTok             | $25 / MTok             |"}
{"id": "e229", "source": "d8", "locator": "§How refusals are billed", "quote": "**Mid-stream refusals:** A mid-stream refusal bills the input tokens and the output already streamed at normal rates."}
{"id": "e230", "source": "d8", "locator": "§Fallback", "quote": "Server-side fallback and the SDK middleware apply fallback credit for you."}
{"id": "e231", "source": "s1", "locator": "§1.5 p13", "quote": "Claude Opus 5.5 for a narrow set of capabilities related to developing frontier LLMs, such as kernel development on certain ML accelerators, similar to our"}
{"id": "e232", "source": "d4", "locator": "§input_transformations", "quote": "In the Message Batches API, an item that leaves the field unset doesn't fail. Where the API enforces the check by default, it drops the failing blocks instead."}
{"id": "e233", "source": "d4", "locator": "§Add or remove tools", "quote": "change which tools the model can use by appending a `role: \"system\"` message that carries `tool_addition` or `tool_removal` blocks."}
{"id": "e234", "source": "d4", "locator": "§Add or remove tools", "quote": "need the beta header `inline-tools-2026-09-15`, which is available on the Claude API."}
{"id": "e235", "source": "d7", "locator": "§Safeguard refusals", "quote": "If your prompts ask the model to write out its reasoning in the response, remove those instructions, set `display: \"summarized\"`, and read the summarized reasoning from the thinking blocks instead"}
{"id": "e236", "source": "d6", "locator": "§Rate limits", "quote": "When your fast mode rate limit is exceeded, the API returns a `429` error with a `retry-after` header indicating when capacity will be available."}
{"id": "e237", "source": "d6", "locator": "§Falling back to standard speed", "quote": "Falling back from fast to standard speed will result in a [prompt cache](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching) miss. Requests at different speeds do not share cached prefixes."}
{"id": "e238", "source": "s1", "locator": "Figure 3.4.2.A p57 (렌더링)", "quote": "Violative vulnerability discovery, classifier flag rate (higher is better): Claude Sonnet 5 43.8%, Claude Opus 5 99.0%, Claude Fable 5.1 98.9%, Claude Opus 5.5 96.8%"}
{"id": "e239", "source": "d3", "locator": "§comparison table", "quote": "| [Retirement](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/model-deprecations)                         | Not sooner than September 1, 2027                                                 | Not sooner than September 22, 2027"}
