{"id": "e241", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.1 p86", "quote": "For Claude Opus 5.5, 18% of rollouts were served by Claude Opus 4.8 after a classifier-triggered fallback, compared to 23% for Claude Fable 5.1."}
{"id": "e242", "source": "s1", "locator": "§5.2.1 p86", "quote": "These fallbacks were concentrated in coding scenarios, where 46% of Claude Opus 5.5’s rollouts fell back, compared to 2% in tool use and under 1% in computer use."}
{"id": "e243", "source": "s1", "locator": "§8.4 Figure 8.4.A p176", "quote": "The result files carry no uncertainty intervals, so none are shown; Cognition's published plots report error bars."}
{"id": "e244", "source": "s1", "locator": "§8.4 p176", "quote": "Scores decline above medium effort but mostly recover at max, as the note above describes."}
{"id": "e245", "source": "hn49818118", "locator": "comment 49818118 (persedes, 2026-09-23T16:01:58Z)", "quote": "Again seeing how max is a clear outlier, the median cost saving is ~38%, not that far off from the proclaimed 40%."}
{"id": "e246", "source": "hn49809918", "locator": "comment 49809918 (nl, 2026-09-23T00:04:15Z)", "quote": "The biggest proportional difference seems to be at max (5.5 is 38% more) and at high (5.5 is 21% less)."}
{"id": "e247", "source": "r1", "locator": "t3_1wnejyx (TigerConsistent, 2026-09-22T16:38:34Z)", "quote": "Opus 5.5 now has a Max effort mode that uses 6x usage. So if Anthropic benchmarks Opus on Max, but subscribers mostly run Medium/High because Max nukes their limits"}
{"id": "e248", "source": "r1", "locator": "t1_pbecs9b (rlemmie, 2026-09-22T16:54:34Z)", "quote": "Notwithstanding anything else, the \"6x or more\" is just a consequence of making \"medium\" default, rather than \"high\"."}
{"id": "e249", "source": "hn49805358", "locator": "comment 49805358 (bleonard, 2026-09-22T17:50:50Z)", "quote": "All of the previous models across major providers had a 10% cache read cost (vs normal cost) and not this is 5%"}
{"id": "e250", "source": "hn49805086", "locator": "comment 49805086 (hedgehog, 2026-09-22T17:34:11Z)", "quote": "In my mix it's usually 98% or 99% at which point Fable 5.1 was pretty close to the same cost as Opus 5 due to the cheaper cached read."}
{"id": "e251", "source": "d2", "locator": "§Prompt caching", "quote": "On Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1, a cache hit costs 2.5% of the standard input price ($0.25 USD per million tokens)."}
{"id": "e252", "source": "hn49810898", "locator": "comment 49810898 (rmunn, 2026-09-23T02:26:19Z)", "quote": "It responded \"You were right to push on this: four of the five line numbers were wrong, and while checking them I found two findings that were overstated.\""}
{"id": "e253", "source": "hn49810898", "locator": "comment 49810898 (rmunn, 2026-09-23T02:26:19Z)", "quote": "Then I noticed in the corner of the Claude CLI UI that it was showing \"Effort: medium\"."}
{"id": "e254", "source": "hn49813778", "locator": "comment 49813778 (narmiouh, 2026-09-23T10:05:10Z)", "quote": "It is interesting that Fable 5.1 max [1] which also produced a decent pelican with 65k output tokens compared to 5.5 running out of 128k output tokens"}
{"id": "e255", "source": "hn49804862", "locator": "comment 49804862 (simonw, 2026-09-22T17:22:51Z)", "quote": "So that failed attempt on max cost me $2.56."}
{"id": "e256", "source": "hn49808591", "locator": "comment 49808591 (mintik, 2026-09-22T21:44:52Z)", "quote": "Quite literally not a single task was able to complete today without getting flagged for [cyber]"}
{"id": "e257", "source": "hn49816280", "locator": "comment 49816280 (rolandf, 2026-09-23T13:57:40Z)", "quote": "By the way any tips on making Opus 5.5 hardening the security of your applications without falling back on 4.8 ?"}
{"id": "e258", "source": "hn49804997", "locator": "comment 49804997 (arw0n, 2026-09-22T17:29:17Z)", "quote": "It has far less false positives now, and generally accepts defensive requests."}
{"id": "e259", "source": "hn49821786", "locator": "comment 49821786 (jdw64, 2026-09-23T20:08:31Z)", "quote": "I'm subscribed to Max 5x, and with the previous Opus 5, I didn't usually hit the 5-hour limit even when doing the same tasks"}
{"id": "e260", "source": "hn49815025", "locator": "comment 49815025 (solsson, 2026-09-23T12:21:32Z)", "quote": "On MacOS the command kills every process with \"cat\" in it. I was using effort high and auto mode."}
{"id": "e261", "source": "s1", "locator": "§6.5.2 p126", "quote": "in absolute terms, destructiveness remained rare—we flag fewer than 1% of recent model sessions."}
{"id": "e262", "source": "x1", "locator": "post 2102440897317064916 (2026-09-22T16:52:26Z)", "quote": "Uses the most tokens per Intelligence Index task of any model benchmarked."}
{"id": "e263", "source": "a1", "locator": "summary", "quote": "When evaluating the Intelligence Index, it generated 260M tokens, which is very verbose in comparison to the median of 88M."}
